/*
  SafetyHistoryWidget.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 dashboard widget · 0084 · SafetyHistoryWidget (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. Every key the native
  `SafetyHistoryWidget` resolves (table "SafetyHistoryWidget") lives here with its web
  English value. These entries fold into the app `Localizable.xcstrings` master
  catalog at integration time; they are kept in a per-surface table so each parallel
  surface prompt owns its own strings without editing the shared catalog.

  The first group holds the keys extracted verbatim from the web source
  (features/dashboard/widgets/SafetyHistoryWidget.tsx) and the dashboard i18n catalog
  (web/src/i18n/en.json): the widget title, the stat labels, the trend words, and the
  empty-feed message. The web `classifySnapshot` titles + `buildSubtitle` fragments +
  `typeLabels` are hardcoded literals in the web source; the native port routes them
  through this table (with the exact web English as the fallback value) so the Swift
  view holds no literals. The remaining keys back the native-only chrome (freshness
  chip, refresh/retry/empty/error copy, accessibility).
*/

